NASA HUNCH Raspberry Pi Server Farm

This project has two main parts:
1. `Cluster/`: monitoring and maintenance stack (Prometheus, Grafana, backend, exporters).
2. `deployer/`: generic app hosting deployer for queued app contracts.

The deployer is now designed to host:
1. Standard web/backend container apps.
2. AI apps (scheduled onto AI-labeled nodes).
3. Apps built from a Git repo containing a Dockerfile.

Prerequisites (on manager node):
1. Docker + Swarm initialized.
2. Python 3 + `pip install pyyaml`.
3. Node labels set for your Pi hardware layout.

Recommended labels for your cluster (2 x 8GB Pi 5, 3 x 4GB Pi 5):
1. Label the two 8GB nodes as AI-capable:
   `docker node update --label-add role=ai <node-name>`
2. Label the three 4GB nodes as general:
   `docker node update --label-add role=general <node-name>`

Deploy monitoring stack:
1. Build images from inside `Cluster/`:
   `docker build -t cluster_sensor_exporter ./simulated_nodes`
   `docker build -t cluster_backup_service ./backup_service`
   `docker build -t cluster_disk_health ./disk_health`
   `docker build -t cluster_manager ./cluster_manager`
   `docker build -t cluster_test_stress ./test_stress`
   `docker build -t cluster_log_aggregator ./log_aggregator`
2. Deploy stack:
   `docker stack deploy -c docker-stack.yml cluster`

Test generic hosting feature (safe dry run first):
1. From repo root:
   `python deployer/deployer.py --queue-dir queue --dry-run`
2. If output looks correct, run real deploy:
   `python deployer/deployer.py --queue-dir queue`

Queue examples:
1. `queue/sample_web.yaml` (web app image)
2. `queue/sample_ai.yaml` (AI app image, role=ai placement)
3. `queue/sample_git_app.yaml` (build image from Git repo)

Verify deployments:
1. `docker service ls`
2. `docker service ps test-web`
3. `docker service ps test-ai-ollama`

Stop cluster stack:
1. `docker stack rm cluster`

Run unit tests:
1. `pytest -v deployer/test_deployer.py`
